# round 79 (w98): the class token through the perturbation operator (--perturb-cls, ported 2026-09-20). Until now the class token was the encoding of the unperturbed graph, across-strain sd exactly 0, so the pooled head read the genotype through the perturbed-gene pool alone; with the flag the token is strain-specific (smoke: sd 0.184). No parameters added. Arms, six seeds each on the released split, both paired by seed against the same cell without the flag: pathlogcls = the round-33 layer-free cell (against w49, 0.908); pathpoolcls = the plain pooled cell with no solve and no affine (against w39_pathpool, 0.860). The read, fixed here: the seed-mean held-out AUROC, the paired difference with its sign count, and cls_strain_sd from the epoch rows.
ESS_ARM=pooled ESS_HIDDEN=12 ESS_HEADS=4 ESS_LAYERS=1 ESS_PREPROC=1 ESS_EPOCHS=200 ESS_BATCH=32 ESS_POSW=1 ESS_SPLIT=ess_fcl_val0.2_s0.json.gz ESS_SEED=2703 ESS_TAG=_w98pathlogcls ESS_OUT=w98_pathlogcls_h12l1p1_e200_s2703 ESS_EXTRA='--node-embeddings pathways prot_T5_all --ess-readout fba --ess-solve-features pfba --ess-solve-encoding log1p --perturb-cls'
